1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,000
When product information lives inside messages, every buyer starts the same conversation again.

2
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:15,000
Staff may keep resending photos, dimensions and material details before the customer can shortlist an option.

3
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:25,000
I designed Formhaus to make that first stage visual, structured and easier to navigate.

4
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:38,000
Buyers can search the range and filter by product category.

5
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:50,000
Each product gives the details needed to compare options, and suitable items can be added to one shortlist.

6
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:59,000
The final enquiry keeps the selected products together, giving sales a clearer starting point for follow-up.

7
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:07,000
This is working proof of the discovery and enquiry flow. It does not claim live inventory, checkout or measured sales results.

8
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:15,000
If your catalogue still lives in DMs or PDFs, let’s design a better buying journey.
